# hwe-bench case allowlist — what the public mirror publishes.
#
# One <track>/<subdomain>/<case-id> per line, relative to `cases/`. Lines
# starting with # are comments; blank lines are ignored. `publish_oss.py`
# reads this and nothing else to decide which case directories reach the
# public mirror.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this list is, as of 2026-08-13
#
# **The public set is the scored set.** The list below is exactly the cases the
# published leaderboard is computed over — one representative per physics
# family, on the three tracks the board reports — so a lab that reads a number
# on hwe-bench.svdailab.com can pull the tasks that number was measured on and
# reproduce it. That is a deliberate reversal of the older rule ("the score is
# published, the cases are not"), taken by the owner on 2026-08-13, and it
# supersedes the #395 reading of this file as a small shop window.
#
# Two things follow, and neither is a defect to be repaired later:
#
#  - **The board is now contaminable.** These tasks are on the public internet
#    from this date, so a model trained after it may have seen them. A future
#    board that wants to claim otherwise needs cases held back from this list,
#    not a caveat added to the page.
#  - **What stays private is the rest of each family.** A track's family holds
#    many operating points and only its representative is here — battery
#    publishes 34 of 50 directories, combustion 21 of 52. The inventory sold
#    for post-training is the unpublished remainder plus the tracks that never
#    reached the board (packaging is out of this list for that reason, not
#    because anything is wrong with it).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules that did not change
#
#  - Only open-source-solver cases. Commercial-solver cases (COMSOL, Fluent,
#    CFX, Abaqus, ...) NEVER go here — they are Path B.
#  - A case under an underscore-prefixed directory (`_pending/`, `_phase2/`,
#    `_deferred/`, `_template/`) is not live and never goes here.
#  - ENFORCED: every entry must resolve to an existing case directory, on a
#    live track, whose task.toml says `release_status = "public_runnable"`.
#  - ENFORCED: `public-runnable-budget` below caps how many live cases may
#    carry `release_status = "public_runnable"` at all.
#
# Check both without touching the mirror:
#     python tools/publish_oss.py --check
# CI runs exactly that. To publish, after the check is green:
#     python tools/publish_oss.py --prune-cases
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# public-runnable-budget: 85
#
# Raised from 51 in the same commit that flipped 35 board cases off
# `public_draft`. The flip is bookkeeping rather than a decision: SCHEMA.md
# defines `public_draft` as "lacks enough runnable assets for the main
# leaderboard", and every one of those 35 is on the main leaderboard with a
# passing oracle, so the marker was describing a state that had stopped being
# true. The budget still does its job — it is why that flip is one line a
# reviewer can see instead of 35 silent edits (#339).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

